
This illustrates the classic FEP mutation of OPLS-UA methanol
to ethane, as in J Chem Phys 83, 3050 (1985). The principal
difference is that 210 TIP4P water molecules are used here for 
the solvent instead of the 125 in the JCP paper. We no longer
have the smaller water box handy; the minimum size of stored
water boxes in BOSS is 216.

For UNIX, the entire FEP is run by submission of just the fepcmd file.
However, the DOS command language is less flexible, so for Windows,
the jobs are chained together using the five .bat files - just
submit f10.bat.
 
Five windows are executed with delta lambda = +- 0.10.
Each window has 1M configurations of equilibration and 2M
of averaging.

The feppar0 and feppar files here are for use with the OPLS-UA force
field. Use the files in the fepaq directory for OPLS-AA.

Time required: 5.8 hours on an R5000 SGI.
               22 minutes on a 2.4 GHz Pentium IV.

