Or use the xSUMDELG or xSUMDW scripts.

Note2: The subdirectory fepaq contains updated cmd file with a
delta lambda of 0.05 and longer averaging (10M per window). 
Scripts are provided for
easy execution of FEP calculations in water.

Note3: The subdirectory fepgas contains the cmd files and scripts for
easy execution of FEP calculations in the gas phase.

Note4: The subdirectory PhXtoY illustrates execution of both gas-phase and
aqueous FEP calculations for conversion of substituted benzenes                   
with full flexibility of the solute. The difference in free energies of
hydration for the two molecules is computed with the OPLS-AA force field.

Note5: The file f010cmd for UNIX/Linux is provided to illustrate a command file
to execute just one step of an FEP calculation. One could generate manually
additional command files (f030cmd, f050cmd, f070cmd, f090cmd)
that can be called in order starting with the submission of
f010cmd to complete a full FEP calculation. fepcmd automates this process.
If one wants to run the five windows on five different computers
simultaneously, submit the five separate cmd files
(f010cmd, f030cmd, f050cmd, f070cmd, f090cmd). Each needs
to use feppar0 as the par file.

Note5: ArtoAr illustrates FEP calculations between azines.
